# Git commits — no Cursor co-author

When creating git commits for this repo:

- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `cursoragent@cursor.com`, or any Cursor agent attribution to commit messages.
- Prefer low-level commit creation when the environment auto-appends co-authors: write the message to a file, then use Git's `commit-tree` (via `Git\mingw64\libexec\git-core\git.exe` on Windows if the wrapper injects trailers) with only the user's author identity.
- Do not use `git commit` if it would append Cursor co-author metadata.
- Only create commits when the user explicitly asks.
